e-wrap;">Puneet Kala</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 2pt 2pt 2pt 2pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">PK</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 2pt 2pt 2pt 2pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 3pt 3pt 3pt 3pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.44; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Roboto; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Dimitris Grammatiko</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 2pt 2pt 2pt 2pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">DG</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 2pt 2pt 2pt 2pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 3pt 3pt 3pt 3pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.44; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Roboto; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Other Attendees:</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 2pt 2pt 2pt 2pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">na</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 2pt 2pt 2pt 2pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Roboto; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> &nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: middle; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.75pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 26pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The Topics</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Update about previous work</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">In the last meeting Kasun was about to develop a mock plugin for test Cloud filesystem with </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Joomla!. </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">You can find it </span><a href="https://github.com/joomla-projects/media-manager-improvement/pull/276" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">here</span></a><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">. Feel free to test and give a feedback. This is a dropbox plugin. So you may want to have a dropbox account for test the Media Manager</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">OAuth2.0 Helper for Joomla!</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Almost all 3rd party developers uses </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">OAuth2.0 </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">for authentication and authorization purposes for Clouds. Allon and David suggested to let those users have a Callback to use for the ease of development as was in the schedule for </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Authentication Process</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">. This callback procedure is described below.</span></p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Proposal for Authentication Helpers</span></h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Introduction</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">For the authorization process it would be nice if we add some helpers for 3rd party developers. This method should be able to be flexible as much as possible because each of plugin acts differently on the </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">OAuth2</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> Process.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Define an Interface</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">For the callbacks provided by the Joomla for developers work, certain methods are required. So it will be better if we could add an interface for the Media Manager to keep the promise between </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Joomla! </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">and the Developer.</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space: pre;"> </span></span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/8tJku7gOFtnirRAJrxq8HLIz19amwC5eBdvmVCRonJDAfQADfPKewihdXw7Xq_BUVomCQhmBD6ldmhcbfajWD4N0CQY76i1hWmO8jZpty8LKwSdszbBD78S1qR_II2yVGodwoOuI" alt="" width="624" height="416" style="border: none; transform: rotate(0.00rad); -webkit-transform: rotate(0.00rad);" /></span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Typically an OAuth Process involves </span></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; margin-left: 36pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Authentication</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; margin-left: 36pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Authorization</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Both of them passes a data for a pre defined redirect url in the provider settings. </span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">For example Dropbox users can get a code after pressing </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Allow </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">for app which can be used to get an access and refresh token.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">So the redirect url is used two times in the Dropbox, which comes with different parameters for each call. One with the </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Access Code </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">and other with </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Access/Refresh Token</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">. The interface we design should developer use the parameters which are passed to the callback for further process.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Interface : </span><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">OAuth2Handler</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<div dir="ltr" style="margin-left: 0pt;">\r\n<table style="border: none; border-collapse: collapse;"><colgroup><col width="354" /></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #999999; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 1pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">OAuth2Handler</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 1pt;">\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">onCallback($params : array)</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The plugins which implements this interface will have the opportunity to use the Cloud Callbacks provided by joomla.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Endpoint for OAuth</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">For this we need an public endpoint for joomla. Best suggestion is to use </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">com_media </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">controller as the endpoint without any involving of </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">JRouter.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">[site-name]/administrator/index.php?option=com_media&amp;task=plugin.oauth2callback&amp;plugin=[plugin-name]</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Can be used as the endpoint for plugins.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">For </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">plg_filesystem_dropbox </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">it would be</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">[</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">site-name/administrator]/index.php?option=com_media&amp;task=plugin.oauth2callback&amp;plugin=plg_filesystem_dropbox</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">So we need to inform developers to use this endpoint</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Process</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">After doing a proper authentication or an authorization, provider pass the required data to the given redirect uri as a GET or POST. In here Joomla will receive all the </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">inputs</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> from that and </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">pass</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> them to relative plugin. </span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">For that Joomla will look for relevant plugin name and pass the data to the method </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">onCallback($params : array)</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">. So the developer can use them either for authentication or authorization depends on the situation.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Security</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">With this setup anyone can send requests and invoke plugins which is a security flaw. Almost all clouds support adding an option called </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">status </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">in the parameters for ensure </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">CSRF </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">is valid. So we must warn developer to set this status to </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">CSRF </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">token in joomla before requesting the Provider. So after processing the result provider will redirect to callback with the </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">status </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">parameter set by the developer. In that case before do anything Joomla will check for it to ensure that it was sent within Joomla!</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">If </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">CSRF </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">check is failed, the request to invoke callback will be rejected.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;"><br /><br /></b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Discussion</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Allon and Yves both agreed on having this endpoint for joomla. Kasun initially decided it to be a public endpoint, but as most providers support </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">status </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">parameter in their cloud authentication process he decided to make this an administrator endpoint. </span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Kasun suggested showing an error message in any error.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">All topics on the above brief introduction was accounted and approved by both mentors.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;"><br /><br /></b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Documentation for Media Manager Joomla!</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Kasun asked Allon about the documentation for the New Media Manager. Allon suggested few ideas how it should be. Yves said he will help Kasun when he start writing it.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Arial; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Final Thoughts</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Kasun will develop the authentication helper and deliver progress in the next meeting</span></p>\r\n<p><br /><br /></p>', NULL, 1, 323, 1, 2498, '2017-08-15 12:48:41', 0, '2017-08-15 12:49:29', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(637, 0, 21, 'Trademark Team Report - August 15, 2017', 'trademark-team-report-august-15-2017', '<p><em>This report is to announce the progress of Trademark &amp; Licensing Team, no meeting has been held today.</em></p>\r\n<h3>Progress &amp; Achievements</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jenn Gress and Deb Cinkus are draining down the Ticket queue, processing all the open tickets.</li>\r\n<li>3 volunteers applied after the Call for Volunteers.</li>\r\n<li>Subodh Mahant, Ugur Uygur and Claire Mandville have been onboarded as Contributors to the Trademark &amp; Licensing Team.</li>\r\n<li>New members are being trained and are reviewing the Trademark material, including the Brand Manual.</li>\r\n<li>Claire has an extended knowledge on TM since she was in charge as leader for TM in the past. She\'s sharing lot of suggestions and helping members in training with TM rules.</li>\r\n<li>Claire and Luca are working to setup a clear framework to deal with trademark/domain requests.</li>\r\n<li>A new trademark audit form is under construction to allow members to properly analyze domain name requests and keep records without spending too much effort on that.</li>\r\n<li>The call for volunteers will be open, so new volunteers are welcome to join us in this rebuilding process!</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, 1, 324, 1, 669, '2017-08-15 14:23:00', 0, '2017-08-15 14:38:46', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(638, 0, 13, '15th August 2017 JUG Team Meeting Minutes', '15th-august-2017-jug-team-meeting-minutes', '<p><strong>In attendance:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Djamel Kherbi<br />Jenn Gress<br />Brian Ronnow<br />Noemi Sanchez del Rio</p>\r\n<p><strong>No shows:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Eric Lamy<br />Rowan (but she doesn\'t really have to be there every meeting anyways)</p>\r\n<p>Went over pending listings of which there are only one. All good.</p>\r\n<p>We are starting the directory review again. It\'s an ongoing and slow process but slow and steady wins the race!</p>\r\n<p>Adding Associations to the directory is taking a back seat until (probably) after JWC. There is much to work out on the rules and terms for them and we need to take the time to do it right and not just wing it. Resources are limited until after JWC.</p>\r\n<p>Next meeting is 5 September and Djamel will lead. Jenn will take minutes.</p>', NULL, 1, 325, 1, 535, '2017-08-15 17:40:25', 0, '2017-08-15 17:44:03', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(639, 0, 10, 'News from the Joomla! Social Media Team', 'news-from-the-joomla-social-media-team', '<p>On August 7th, and after many years of service, Sigrid resigned her position of Social Media Team Leader.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The team have since done an election and effective August 21st I will be the new Team Lead with Hans Van Der Meer as my Assistant. Sandra Thevenet will continue to help and guide the team and I am pleased to welcome back Mike Veeckmans who will be assisting us with copywriting.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Thank you again, Sigrid, for all you have done, and wishing you much happiness. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Team Lead: Alison Meeks</p>\r\n<p>Assistant Team Lead: Hans Van Der Meer</p>\r\n<p>Member: Sandra Thevenet</p>\r\n<p>Contributor: Mike Veeckmans &nbsp;</p>', NULL, 1, 326, 1, 621, '2017-08-20 17:10:14', 0, '2017-08-20 17:18:15', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(640, 58, 0, 'OSM, Inc. - Full Board Meeting - August 17, 2017', 'osm-inc-full-board-meeting-august-17-2017', '<h2 id="docs-internal-guid-a01adc30-0534-f72f-dce1-ea7a9a0c1923" dir="ltr" style="text-align: center;">Open Source Matters, Inc.<br />Full Board of Directors and Officers Meeting</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Date</span>: August 17, 2017</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Time</span>: 17:00 UTC</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Total time of meeting</span>: 1 hour 25 minutes</p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr">Attendees:</h4>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert Jacobi (President), Aleksander Kuczek (Vice President), Luca Marzo (Secretary), Mike Demopoulos (Treasurer), Rowan Hoskyns-Abrahall (Director), Michael Babker (Director), Radek Suski (Director), Yves Hoppe (Director), Peter Martin (Director), Søren Beck Jensen (Director).</p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr">Apologies:</h4>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Discussion outline</h2>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">President</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert, Mike and Rowan shared progress about WHD preparation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Production Department Report</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Tom Hutchinson replaced Sandra Thevenet as Documentation Team Leader.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">George Wilson to be appointed Team Leader of the CMS Maintenance Team.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Framework Team will be marked as “In Formation” while looking for a new Team Lead and other volunteers.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Joomla! 3.7.5 release addressed a bug with remote databases introduced by 3.7.4. No changes in production websites.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Joomla! 3.8 is on schedule.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Production Department will have a meeting in person during JWC.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Further details in the Production Department Meeting minutes shared by Michael: <a href="departments/production/reports/633-8-aug-2017-team-lead-meeting">https://volunteers.joomla.org/departments/production/reports/633-8-aug-2017-team-lead-meeting</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Legal &amp; Finance Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">RFP process for Google Domains has been extended.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Trademark Team onboarded new contributors and the restructuring process is on its way. <a href="teams/trademark-team/reports/637-trademark-team-report-august-15-2017">https://volunteers.joomla.org/teams/trademark-team/reports/637-trademark-team-report-august-15-2017</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Marketing &amp; Communication Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The new elected Marketing &amp; Communication Department Coordinator is Sandra Decoux (Thevenet). The new Marketing and Communication Department Coordinator will begin her term starting September 23, 2017.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan and Yves shared progress reports on Strategic Marketing Plan from Market Accents and PR Provision from The Right Image.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan discussed possible 12th Birthday Swag Campaign. Decision will be made within next few days as to how to proceed.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Events Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JWC has had a responsibilities shuffle and is now operating at full speed. &nbsp;With banking reenabled can now start some paid social campaigns to improve Italian momentum.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jenn Gress is doing a fantastic job with speakers and around 50% of the confirmed talks including keynotes will be released starting next week.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sponsorship is coming in at a decent rate, sold packages are now marked clearly on the sponsorship micro website.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JWC Attendance of team members under department is being finalised. Rowan shared a spreadsheet with DC’s for them to allocate their numbers for JWC attendance.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Now have access to monitoring JoomlaDay financial support requests to both smooth approval process and tally funds spent to date in year.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">CMS Africa Sponsorship will be paid shortly.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Operations Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Board discussed about the update policy and responsibility for Joomla.org properties.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan is working on a manual that includes the standard policies, operating procedures and best practices for the project’s properties.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Board discussed about the current situation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Programs Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JET started and closing in 2 days. &nbsp;18 Applications received so far.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Peakon Meeting + VET Sprint (Rowan and Yves) in London 9th to 13th August.<br /><a href="teams/volunteer-engagement-team/reports/635-peakon-kick-off-meeting-sprint">https://volunteers.joomla.org/teams/volunteer-engagement-team/reports/635-peakon-kick-off-meeting-sprint</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">First survey going out end of August</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Certification Program will launch the italian version of the Administrator Exam at the Joomla! World Conference in Rome.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Vice President</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Aleksander is working on the Contributor agreements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Secretary</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Group 1 Election Process completed. Results have been published to the Community Portal.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Officer Election Results for the records: <a href="https://goo.gl/WCrNR9">https://goo.gl/WCrNR9</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Following the Joomla! Election Cycle policy document, new Board members will enter &nbsp;the handover/transition period and will start in official capacity on September 23, 2017.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Transparency Report has been published. <a href="https://community.joomla.org/blogs/leadership/3134-joomla-officer-elections-transparency-report.html">https://community.joomla.org/blogs/leadership/3134-joomla-officer-elections-transparency-report.html</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan, Yves and Luca worked on the Global Privacy Policy to include the necessary consents to operate the Volunteers Engagement Program, Sandra published it.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Privacy Policy Update notice has been sent to all Project’s Active Volunteers through the Volunteers Portal on August 12, 2017.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Start to recruit an Ombudsman, which will be responsible for all the impartial matters, like the election.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Luca to prepare the Election Framework, set of documents, suggestions, best-practices and lessons learned about the Group 1 Election. This set of recommendation, documents and tools will be provided to the Ombudsman to properly manage the election.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Since the GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) of the European Union will be effective since May 25, 2018, the Project has to evaluate the impact of such regulation and update its privacy policy and internal process accordingly.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Treasurer</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">New accounts are almost done.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">New checks have been ordered.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Mike shared also some updates on the banking issue.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Mike is working on taxes, statements to be submitted for approval in the next days.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Mike and Rowan will improve the reimbursement form with extra fields regarding wire transfer, to save money on transfer fees. These improvements will also increase the security and protect the Project.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Other business</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan proposed to have an in person Board Meeting before the JWC 2017 in Rome.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Radek reminded the importance of keeping team listings up to date.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Motions taken during this meeting</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017/054 - Allow Sandra Thevenet, the new elected Marketing &amp; Communication Department Coordinator to attend the next Board Meeting.</strong> <br />Proposed by Søren Beck Jensen, seconded by Radek Suski<br /><em>The motion passed with unanimous consent.</em></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017/055 - Assign Super User Access to the Volunteers Portal to the Secretary, Yves and Rowan to manage the Volunteers Engagement Program.</strong> <br />Proposed by Yves Hoppe, seconded by Luca Marzo<br /><em>The motion passed with unanimous consent.</em></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017/056 - Create an informal Working Group under the Legal Department to work on the Privacy Policy and Data Protection for the GDPR.</strong> <br />Proposed by Luca Marzo, Seconded by Yves Hoppe<br /><em>The motion passed with unanimous consent.</em></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017/057 - Organize an in person Board Meeting on Wednesday November 15, 2017 before the Joomla! World Conference.</strong><br />Proposed by Rowan Hoskyns-Abrahall, Seconded by Luca Marzo<em><br />The motion passed with unanimous consent and 1 abstention.</em></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017/058 - The Secretary proposes to adjourn the meeting<br /></strong>Proposed by Luca Marzo, seconded by Yves Hoppe.<br /><em>The motion passed with unanimous consent.</em></p>', NULL, 1, 327, 2, 669, '2017-08-21 14:31:52', 669, '2017-08-21 14:43:50', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(641, 0, 109, '11th Meeting Joomla! GSoC 2017: JDocs Help Screens', '11th-meeting-joomla-gsoc-2017-jdocs-help-screens', '<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 3pt;">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Date: 17th August 2017</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Time: 16:00 (UTC / GMT)</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Meeting was attended by: Sandra Thevenet, Shivam Rajput, Tom Hutchison, Yves Hoppe, Peter Martin</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<ol style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Guided Tour Update(</span><a href="https://github.com/joomla-projects/gsoc17_helpscreens_on_jdocs/tree/jsontest" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">https://github.com/joomla-projects/gsoc17_helpscreens_on_jdocs/tree/jsontest</span></a><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">).</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The current state of the Guided Tour is that I have done the editing of that and it is almost ready to be made to the Joomla core.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Asked Suggestion from the team regarding the Guided Tour repo.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Currently, two suggestion suggested by Joao.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">1) lang. String</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.6363636363636362; text-indent: 17pt; margin: 0pt 19pt 0pt 19pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">2) some correction of the running instruction.</span></p>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<ol start="2" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Screenshot-Automation Update(</span><a href="https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B1eYyialFUnoYl9aMUtWUS1za00" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B1eYyialFUnoYl9aMUtWUS1za00</span></a><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">)</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The screenshot Automation is almost done some of the testing, code style and comments are to done.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The link mentioned above are some of the updated Screenshot taken using the Screenshot Repo.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<ol start="3" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Final Blog Update(</span><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1p-b8VYpNRzMOqIUZYjD9h7mqOh0it0tWQNnT_XJgs7w/edit?usp=drive_web" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1p-b8VYpNRzMOqIUZYjD9h7mqOh0it0tWQNnT_XJgs7w/edit?usp=drive_web</span></a><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">)</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The Final Blog is made and some suggestion suggested by Joao and Peter are to made.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Blog deadline i.e 15 August 2017.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<ol start="4" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Guided Tour PR to the Joomla Core.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">As my 3 rd evaluation is going to be started from 21 August</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><br class="kix-line-break" /></span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">So I request team to put their review over the branch so that I can submit the URL of the PR</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<ol start="5" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Documentation Update for the Guided Tour(</span><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Do800J4TnB5a9Q_xTYkNnppKvUWZDxieoJ0VETV4BzA/edit" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Do800J4TnB5a9Q_xTYkNnppKvUWZDxieoJ0VETV4BzA/edit#</span></a><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> ).</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Already reviewed by Joao and Sandra.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Yea I need to add extension screenshot too</span><a href="https://app.glip.com/" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> João Reys Santos</span></a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">.Requested from Tom and Peter to Review this also.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<ol start="6" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Documentation Update for the Screenshot Automation( </span><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WgIxfFTGm1nPlRjBjJaZV0z_ip1WcMSVYaHKLVdRiBA/edit" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WgIxfFTGm1nPlRjBjJaZV0z_ip1WcMSVYaHKLVdRiBA/edit</span></a><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> ).</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Started with this asked Sandra for some suggestion how I should proceed.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, 1, 328, 1, 2497, '2017-08-20 15:35:00', 0, '2017-08-21 15:36:04', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(642, 0, 78, ' Certification Steering Meeting - August 22, 2017', 'certification-steering-meeting-august-22-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-4a5f662f-e980-9a72-c965-d65c40184e3d" dir="ltr">The Joomla! Certification Steering Group meets every Tuesday at 1:00 PM GMT. This meeting was held on August 22, 2017 on Glip.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Team members</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>In attendance</em>: Sam Suresh, Luca Marzo, Chris Keen, Andrea Gentil.</p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Discussion Outline</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The Certification Steering Group discussed about the sprint during JWC 17 in Rome. Sam requested subteams to prepare a travel cost estimation for members that will attend such sprint.</li>\r\n<li>Andrea to work on an acknowledgment page to say Thank you to all the companies/professionals who gave us their work/software/services for free.</li>\r\n<li>A new Joomla! Learning Partners Directory is being built on the Certification website.</li>\r\n<li>Certified Users Badge is now displayed on the Joomla! Volunteers Portal.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Operations Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>1 new application as JoomlaDay to be reviewed</li>\r\n<li>1 new application as Joomla! Learning Partner to be reviewed</li>\r\n<li>Queue of applications pending evaluation has been cleaned up</li>\r\n<li>Certification Ambassadors plan awaiting approval from Steering Group</li>\r\n<li>A company would donate time to develop the COT Workflow Extension, further details to come soon.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Platform Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Sam and Chris are working on the QMS</li>\r\n<li>As soon as QMS is ready, we can work on the Italian Translation of the Joomla! Administrator Exam for JWC.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Marketing Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Andrea is working on a newsletter for current JLPs.</li>\r\n<li>Newsletter to go out at the end of this week.</li>\r\n<li>Start promoting september sessions.</li>\r\n<li>Andrea to approach JDDE organizers to have an exam session there.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Exam Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Team discussed about QMS and the use of Custom fields</li>\r\n<li>Team developed a list of guidelines and best practices for new members.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Meeting ends after 40 minutes.</p>', NULL, 1, 329, 1, 669, '2017-08-22 12:26:12', 0, '2017-08-22 12:40:43', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(643, 0, 25, '2017-08 Joomla! Bug Squad Team Meeting', '2017-08', '<p dir="ltr">Friday, August 18th, 2017, 18:00 UTC on Glip</p>\r\n<div dir="ltr">\r\n<table><colgroup><col width="231" /><col width="52" /><col width="29" /><col width="234" /><col width="50" /><col width="28" /></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan="6">\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Attendees</h3>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Niels Braczek</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">NB</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">x</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jacques Rentzke</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Demis Palma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">DP</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jennifer Marriott</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Achal Aggarwal</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Kevin Griffiths</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">André Pereira da Silva</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Klas Berlic</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Anja Hage</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Leo Lammerink</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Beat</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Michael Babker</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">MB</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">x</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Brian Teeman</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Nicholas K. Dionysopoulos</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Chris Davenport</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Nicola Galgano</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Chris Paschen</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Niels van der Veer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Constantin Romankiewicz</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Peter Martin</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">David Steltz</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rishi Vishwakarma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Dimitris Grammatikogiannis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert Deutz</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Duke Speer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Roland Dalmulder</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Franz Wohlkönig</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Ruchika Nagarkar</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">George Wilson</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sandra Thevenet</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">ST</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">x</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Gunjan Patel</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Shreyas B</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Hannes Papenberg</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Tarun Jacob</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Harald Leithner</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Thomas Hunziker</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Hervé Boinnard</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Troy Hall</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">TH</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">x</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jean-Marie Simonet</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Yaniv Rozenman</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jacob Waisner</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Yves Hoppe</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">YH</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">x</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Agenda / Minutes</h2>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">1 Purpose, Function and Roles</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>In the new structure of the Joomla! Organisation, each team had to define its purpose, function and roles. The definition was made in coordination with the Product Department Leadership, resulting in the <a href="https://docs.joomla.org/Portal:Bug_Squad/Intro">description on the Volunteers Portal</a>.</em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Tracker and GitHub were not mentioned explicitly. That has been changed.</p>\r\n<p>The Purpose, Function and Roles description was accepted.</p>\r\n<h3>2 Measuring Efford</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>The role of a JBS member has changed. It is not longer sufficient to want to be a member.</em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>That makes it necessary to measure the members’ activity in one way or another. It is possible to get more or less suitable numbers from the tracker itself, it should be possible for the forums as well. However, a whole bunch of expected engagement can’t be measured directly, especially on third party sites like StackOverflow.</em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Until a better solution exists, members are asked to provide a rough monthly summary of their activity. This reporting can be supported by some key persons which know what\'s going on in their sections, like Tobias for GitHub, Sandra for JDocs, Alison for Social Media, etc. It has to be automated in the mid/long term, though.</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Troy found some resources to get numbers from external services, which will be shared with the Joomla! Volunteer Engagement Team (VET).</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">3 Consolidation of Member list</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>Members not meeting the expectations mentioned in the document referenced above for three months, will be moved to the Contributor role instead.</em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>Contributors without any activity on the tracker for three months will be removed from the team.</em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>People with repeating activity on the tracker can be added to the Contributors list.</em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em>Contributors who meet the expectations for a Member, can be promoted to the Members list.</em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">This procedure was accepted.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">4 Test Tools</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The GSoC project “PR Testing Platform” is creating an online tool for PR testing. A prototype can be seen at <a href="https://dbox-tests.ml/">https://dbox-tests.ml/</a>.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">5 Miscellaneous</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Troy is producing a series of bug squashing and development related video tutorials that will be published on JDocs (hosted on Youtube).</p>\r\n<h3>6 Next Meeting</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Regular team meeting each month on the 3rd Friday at 18:00 UTC on Glip.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, 1, 330, 1, 625, '2017-08-23 12:07:17', 0, '2017-08-23 12:16:29', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(644, 0, 44, 'JED Team Meeting - July 28, 2017', 'jed-team-meeting-july-28-2017', '<p class="code-line" style="position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;" data-line="3"><img src="https://cdn.joomla.org/images/sharing/joomla-twitter-card.png" alt="JED Team Meeting - June 30, 2017 " style="max-height: 100%;" /></p>\r\n<p class="code-line" style="position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;" data-line="5">Today the Joomla! Extensions Directory (JED) team met at 2 pm GMT via Glip to discuss our progress of current tasks.</p>\r\n<ul style="color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="7">\r\n<p class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="7"><strong>In attendance</strong>: Jaz Parkyn, Anibal Sanchez, Darek Śnieg, Luca Marzo, Mark Lee and Miron Savan.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="9">\r\n<p class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="9"><strong>Absent</strong>: Aleksander Kuczek, Daniel Dubois, Dénes Székely, Hugh Douglas-Smith, Markus Bopp, Martin Mueller, Paul Franklin and Sotiris Katsaniotis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 id="jed-full-text-search-2017---search-improvements-candidates" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="11">JED 4 - New System Specification</h2>\r\n<ul style="color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="13">\r\n<p id="vel-team-organization" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="56">New JED will start progressing at the beginning of summer. The new JED build process will be formalised first, specifications to be reviewed with the team for comments, additions and amendments, to plan the general development.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="13">\r\n<p id="vel-team-organization" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="56">The reviews and scoring functionality will remain a closed subject and its code will not present to the JED Devs - only available to JED Team Members.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="13"><span style="color: #333333; font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">Jaz has started to plan and define the next version of JED. She\'s been continually working on the specifications doc for the new com_jed, and will soon present it to the team for feedback.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 id="jed-homepage-2017-updates-jorg-220-and-joomla-372" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="40">JED Homepage 2017 updates&nbsp;and Joomla 3.7.2</h2>\r\n<ul style="color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="43">After the update to Joomla 3.7.2, we suffered several outages&nbsp;and we solved them disabling a feature of a recently updated extension. It took several iterations to discovering the source of the performance problems.</li>\r\n<li>Images Cache Drive reached 100% several times. It has been increased and a cleaning task has been scheduled to be performed weekly.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="code-line" style="position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;" data-line="46">Following the initial phase, we are working on the<span class="Apple-converted-space"></span><em>second phase</em>:</p>\r\n<ul style="color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="42">The new design must be applied to other areas of the site. (e.g. the search form located in the inner pages)</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="43"><em>Google Analytics tracking on JED</em>: GA Event tracking implementation will be reviewed. (Alek - Anibal)</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="48">The new homepage has been successfully implemented. Though, more improvements are required.</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="49">Recently Added, Top Rated, Most Viewed modules are coming, on incremental small/new changes.</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="50">New scrolling widgets (similar to Google Play style).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="11">Google Summer of Code 2017: Enhancements to Extension Manager</h2>\r\n<p class="code-line" style="position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;" data-line="33">Anibal has joined the team of mentors, and we are participating in the initial review of the project ideas. The project is progressing well; the first three features are almost completed, reports about the progress can be found here:</p>\r\n<ul style="color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="35"><a href="teams/gsoc-17-expand-extension-manager/reports/588-8th-meeting-gsoc-17-expand-extensions-manager">8th Meeting GSoC 17 - Expand Extensions Manager</a>, by Nuno Lopes</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="35"><a href="teams/gsoc-17-expand-extension-manager/reports/585-7th-meeting-gsoc-17-expand-extensions-manager">7th Meeting GSoC 17 - Expand Extensions Manager</a>, by Nuno Lopes</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="35"><a href="teams/gsoc-17-expand-extension-manager/reports/581-6th-meeting-gsoc-17-expand-extensions-manager">6th Meeting GSoC 17 - Expand Extensions Manager</a>, by Nuno Lopes</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="35"><a href="teams/gsoc-17-expand-extension-manager/reports/569-4th-meeting-gsoc-17-expand-extensions-manager" style="color: #4080d0;">4th Meeting GSoC 17 - Expand Extensions Manager</a>, by Nuno Lopes</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="36"><a href="teams/gsoc-17-expand-extension-manager/reports/553-3rd-meeting-gsoc-17-expand-extensions-manager" style="color: #4080d0;">3rd Meeting GSoC 17 - Expand Extensions Manager</a>, by Nuno Lopes</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="37"><a href="teams/gsoc-17-expand-extension-manager/reports/536-2nd-meeting-gsoc-17-expand-extensions-manager" style="color: #4080d0;">2nd Meeting GSoC 17 - Expand Extensions Manager</a>, by Nuno Lopes</li>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="38"><a href="teams/gsoc-17-expand-extension-manager/reports/527-1st-meeting-gsoc-17-expand-extensions-manager" style="color: #4080d0;">1st Meeting GSoC 17 - Expand Extensions Manager</a>, by Nuno Lopes</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 id="jed-homepage-2017-updates-jorg-220-and-joomla-372" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="40">The Review Checking Process</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The efforts to improve the process are ongoing. We expect further additions in the short term. In JDayUK 2017, we will continue implementing the review process enhancements.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="11">JED Full-Text Search 2017 - Search improvements candidates</h2>\r\n<ul style="color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative;" data-line="13">We are considering Algolia or Elastic Search. No decision yet on the supporting technology.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 id="developer-collaboration-process" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="27">Developer Collaboration Process</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;" data-line="29"><em>Migration to Github</em>: Efforts are continuing in this direction.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, 1, 331, 1, 628, '2017-07-28 19:44:00', 0, '2017-08-23 20:09:39', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(645, 55, 0, 'Joomla Operations Department Meeting, August 23th 2017', 'joomla-operations-department-meeting-august-2017', '<h2 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Joomla Operations Department Meeting</h2>\r\n<p>Wednesday August 23th 2017, 19:00:00 &nbsp;UTC</p>\r\n<p><a name="docs-internal-guid-082be6d3-5c59-adc7-45dd-2c9cbf68fda7"></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Participants:</strong> Jaz Parkyn (Extensions Directory Team), Olaf Offick (Forum Team), Peter Martin (Operations Department Coordinator), Sander Potjer (Volunteers Portal Team), Sławomir Sikora (Template Directory Team), Brian Mitchell (Resource Directory Team).</p>\r\n<p><strong>Invited:</strong>&nbsp;Jacques Rentzke (Community Magazine Team)</p>\r\n<p><strong>Apologies:</strong> Sebastien Lapoux (Showcase Directory Team), Helvecio da Silva (Community Magazine Team)</p>\r\n<h2 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Minutes:</h2>\r\n<h3 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Operations Department Coordinator</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href="board-of-directors/reports/640-osm-inc-full-board-meeting-august-17-2017" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Board of Directors Full Board Meeting - August 17, 2017</a></li>\r\n<li><a href="board-of-directors/reports/623-osm-inc-full-board-meeting-august-03-2017" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Board of Directors Full Board Meeting - August 03, 2017</a></li>\r\n<li><a href="board-of-directors/reports/602-osm-inc-full-board-meeting-july-20-2017" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Board of Directors Full Board Meeting - July 20, 2017</a></li>\r\n<li>We would like to have a better insight in the technical performance of the servers (e.g. in case of technical issues) on which our Joomla.org websites are running. Unfortunately monitoring software like Nagios needs root access to the servers.</li>\r\n<li>Although the Joomla 3.7.5 update was just a bug fix to solve one file in the installation folder (so only necessary for sites that have to be installed), it’s a good practice to keep your site up-to-date. Peter asked the teams to check their Joomla version, and also check if 3rd party extensions are up to date.</li>\r\n<li>At the moment we do not have a Standard Operating Procedure for updating &amp; a backup strategy for Joomla.org sites in place. We need to standardize this.</li>\r\n<li>We try to arrange a face-to-face meeting with the Operations Department team leaders just before JWC on Thursday 16 november 2017.</li>\r\n<li>Team Sprints are a great way to getting things done in a very short period. Peter asked the teams if they had any plans about doing a Team Sprint to improve their joomla.org sites.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Community Magazine Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href="teams/joomla-community-magazine-team/reports/618-jcm-team-meeting-and-updates-report-aug-2017" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JCM Team Meeting and Updates Report: AUG 2017</a></li>\r\n<li>JCM can use some volunteers: authors and proofreaders, see <a href="teams/joomla-community-magazine-team#roles">https://volunteers.joomla.org/teams/joomla-community-magazine-team#roles</a> &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>The Magazine <a href="https://magazine.joomla.org/">https://magazine.joomla.org/</a> &nbsp;needs more community input regarding authors. E.g. “how-to” articles.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Extensions Directory Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The Board has decided to have a single general sponsorship form and not for separate projects/teams. Separate sponsorship forms will complicate the budgeting too much as the received funds can only be used for the cause it raised money for.</li>\r\n<li>JED received a number of forum posts and tickets about disappearing reviews. This has been caused because JED uses an external review checker which could only check the reviews after they had been published. JED is migrating this external review checker over to their own server to improve the extension review process.</li>\r\n<li>The JED team will hold a face-to-face meeting on Thursday 16 November just before the Joomla World Conference (JWC) in Rome.</li>\r\n<li>The JED team is continuing on the specifications document for JED4 (new future version of the Extensions Directory)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Forum Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href="teams/forum-team/reports/619-2017-07-statistics">Forum Statistics - July 2017</a></li>\r\n<li>The Forum Team has contacted its inactive moderators. If they want to continue helping out, they have to respond before 9th September. After that they will be thanked for their past involvement and removed from the moderator team.</li>\r\n<li>After 9th September it will be decided if/which some boards need new moderators</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Resource Directory Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The JRD team is continuing with the specifications for a new improved Joomla Resources Directory.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Template Directory Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href="teams/template-directory-team/reports/606-jtd-meeting-at-july-24th-2017">Report of JTD Meeting at July, 24th, 2017</a></li>\r\n<li>The JTD team welcomed 3 new volunteers to the team</li>\r\n<li>The team has a server ready to start with the development of the new Template Directory</li>\r\n<li>The JRD found a Template Club that is interested in making available their API to their template data which can be used for development of the JTD.</li>\r\n<li>To kickstart the development of the new Template Directory, the team will organize a Team Sprint probably in October/November.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Volunteers Portal Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The JVP team worked with the Volunteer Engagement Team to implement Peakon-integration on the Volunteers Portal</li>\r\n<li>A couple of new volunteers applied to help out in the team. The JVP can still use some more volunteers. See: <a href="teams/volunteers-portal-team#roles">https://volunteers.joomla.org/teams/volunteers-portal-team#roles</a> &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>The JVP team asked about a Standard Operating Procedure regarding getting access to Joomla sites and regarding code changes (which should be done via git and not directly in files on the server).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style="font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #333333;">Showcase Directory Team</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Sebastien not present. Carried over to next meeting.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, 1, 332, 6, 443, '2017-08-24 12:11:59', 443, '2017-08-24 12:33:21', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(646, 0, 19, ' COT - Meeting Notes - August 24, 2017', 'cot-meeting-notes-august-24-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-53d459ac-1458-cdfd-7a01-870b694922d2" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The Joomla! Certification Operations Team (COT) meets every Thursday at 1:00 PM GMT. This meeting was held on August 24, 2017, on Glip.</span></p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #434343; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Team members</span></h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #ff9900; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">In attendance</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">: &nbsp;Luca Marzo, Oscar Ortiz, Todd Woodward, Pablo Pantoja, Andrea Gentil, </span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #ff9900; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Absent</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">: &nbsp;Chris Keen, Hector Mansilla, Richard van Tilborg, Arjen Schrijvers</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Discussion Outline</span></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Joomla! Learning Partners Directory. Andrea Gentil is working on it. If available, please help her.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Next week Steering Group will approve our rebranding of the Regional Coordinators into Certification Ambassadors </span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">COT Workflow Extension: some of you applied to help, but we need to work on that since till now, nothing has been done. Most of you are developers; your help is very appreciated.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Processing new JLP applications</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">JVP profile, the new feature to add the badge has to be activated, filling out the "JCP profile" field in the volunteer profile on JVP</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Upcoming exam sessions:</span><a href="https://certification.joomla.org/exam/calendar" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">https://certification.joomla.org/exam/calendar</span></a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">All of these meeting notes are not final and cannot be used as a reference.</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The meeting ends after 25 minutes.</span></p>', NULL, 1, 333, 1, 1459, '2017-08-24 13:03:50', 0, '2017-08-24 13:07:14', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(647, 0, 114, 'Contributor Agreement Working Group Meeting #2', 'contributor-agreement-working-group-meeting-2', '<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; word-wrap: break-word; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Date</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Aug 24th, 2017 - 14:30-15:00 UTC</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; word-wrap: break-word; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Total time of meeting: 30 minutes.</span></p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.38; color: #333333;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Attendees:</span></h4>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; word-wrap: break-word; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Daliah Saper, Yves Hoppe, Aleksander Kuczek</span></p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.38; color: #333333;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Guests:</span></h4>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; word-wrap: break-word; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: \'Open Sans\';"><span style="font-size: 13.3333px; white-space: pre-wrap;">Rowan Hoskyns Abrahall, Robert Jacobi</span></span><br /></span></p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.38; color: #333333;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #666666; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Apologies:</span></h4>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; word-wrap: break-word; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">-</span></p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.38; color: #333333;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Discussion outline</span></h2>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.38; color: #333333;"><span style="color: #434343; font-family: \'Open Sans\';"><span style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; white-space: pre-wrap;">Why Joomla need contributor agreement?</span></span><a style="color: #000000; font-family: SFNSText, \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; white-space: nowrap;" data-topotext="[{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;tombstoned&quot;:false,&quot;uniqueId&quot;:4,&quot;paragraphStyle&quot;:{&quot;style&quot;:102,&quot;alignment&quot;:0,&quot;writingDirection&quot;:1,&quot;startingListItemNumber&quot;:1}},&quot;codePoints&quot;:[68,111,99,117,109,101,110,116,115,32,97,117,100,105,116,10]},{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;tombstoned&quot;:false,&quot;uniqueId&quot;:5,&quot;paragraphStyle&quot;:{&quot;style&quot;:102,&quot;alignment&quot;:0,&quot;writingDirection&quot;:1}},&quot;codePoints&quot;:[77,101,114,103,101,44,32,114,101,112,104,114,97,115,101,32,97,110,100,32,100,114,97,102,116,32,116,104,101,32,110,101,119,32,111,110,101,40,115,41,10,73,110,116,101,103,114,97,116,101,32,119,105,116,104,32,118,111,108,117,110,116,101,101,114,32,112,111,114,116,97,108,10,80,101,114,102,111,114,109,32,115,105,103,110,105,110,103,32,119,105,116,104,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,99,111,109,109,117,110,105,116,121,32]}]"></a></h3>\r\n<p style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: normal; word-wrap: break-word;">The team has discussed the reasons why Joomla needs a contributor agreement provided by the Board. The team has agreed that we are looking for the easiest possible solution that will cover the areas indicated by the Board.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.38; color: #333333;"><span style="color: #434343; font-family: \'Open Sans\';"><span style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; white-space: pre-wrap;">Suggested solution</span></span><a style="color: #000000; font-family: SFNSText, \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; white-space: nowrap;" data-topotext="[{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;tombstoned&quot;:false,&quot;uniqueId&quot;:4,&quot;paragraphStyle&quot;:{&quot;style&quot;:102,&quot;alignment&quot;:0,&quot;writingDirection&quot;:1,&quot;startingListItemNumber&quot;:1}},&quot;codePoints&quot;:[68,111,99,117,109,101,110,116,115,32,97,117,100,105,116,10]},{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;tombstoned&quot;:false,&quot;uniqueId&quot;:5,&quot;paragraphStyle&quot;:{&quot;style&quot;:102,&quot;alignment&quot;:0,&quot;writingDirection&quot;:1}},&quot;codePoints&quot;:[77,101,114,103,101,44,32,114,101,112,104,114,97,115,101,32,97,110,100,32,100,114,97,102,116,32,116,104,101,32,110,101,119,32,111,110,101,40,115,41,10,73,110,116,101,103,114,97,116,101,32,119,105,116,104,32,118,111,108,117,110,116,101,101,114,32,112,111,114,116,97,108,10,80,101,114,102,111,114,109,32,115,105,103,110,105,110,103,32,119,105,116,104,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,99,111,109,109,117,110,105,116,121,32]}]"></a></h3>\r\n<p style="word-wrap: break-word;">The team has proposed the following solution:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li style="word-wrap: break-word;">Code and other contributions kept in repositories. Enforcing the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO) on all Pull Requests to all Joomla GitHub repositories. This can be done with&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/apps/dco">https://github.com/apps/dco</a>. According to lawyers in the team, the DCO sign-off is sufficient to accept these Pull&nbsp;Request without any additional formalities.</li>\r\n<li>All other contributions. Adding consent to Joomla Contributor Agreement (JCA) as part of the registration process at Joomla Volunteers&nbsp;Portal (potentially&nbsp;joint check box with accepting the Code of Conduct).</li>\r\n<li>Code of Conduct. Adding consent to Code of Conduct (CoC) as part of the registration process at Joomla Volunteers&nbsp;Portal (potentially&nbsp;joint check box with accepting the code of conduct).</li>\r\n<li>Future changes in JCA or CoC will be notified to volunteers, but will not require consent (opt-out).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.38; color: #333333;"><span style="color: #434343; font-family: \'Open Sans\';"><span style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; white-space: pre-wrap;">Next steps</span></span></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style="word-wrap: break-word;">Talking with Production department and other departments about implementing DCO in GitHub repository.</li>\r\n<li>Reviewing the current Joomla Contributor Agreement</li>\r\n<li>Implementing changes in Joomla Volunteers&nbsp;Portal</li>\r\n<li>Making all Joomlers sign updated CoC and JCA on Joomla Volunteers&nbsp;Portal</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, 1, 334, 1, 2317, '2017-08-25 16:32:25', 0, '2017-08-25 16:32:41', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(648, 0, 82, 'Joomla! 3.8 Landing Page - Report August 26, 2017', 'joomla-3-8-landing-page-report-august-26-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-3803cb68-2173-7226-1c15-937e1e476b7f" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Common meeting with the Marketing Product Release Management Team Lead, JDocs Team Lead and Community Translation Assistant Team Lead.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The landing page for Joomla! 3.8 is ready and is already translated into 24 languages thanks to the great work of the CTT Team. </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"><br class="kix-line-break" /></span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Many languages still need some translations: </span><a href="https://crowdin.com/project/joomla-3-landing-page" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">https://crowdin.com/project/joomla-3-landing-page</span></a><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"><br class="kix-line-break" /></span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">All languages have been merged to the repo, all pictures have been created.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The Marketing Product Release Management Team Lead created all the imagery and copywriting for the teasing campaign on Social Media. </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"><br class="kix-line-break" /></span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The Social Media Team started the campaign.&nbsp; </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"><br class="kix-line-break" /></span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The 3.8 teasing imagery is publicly available at &nbsp;</span><a href="https://joom.la/38comingsoon" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">https://joom.la/38comingsoon</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"><br class="kix-line-break" /></span></a><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The 3.8 imagery will be publicly available once 3.8 is released. &nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The JDocs Team Lead created a tutorial for the New Routing System </span><a href="https://docs.joomla.org/J3.x:New_Routing_System" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">https://docs.joomla.org/J3.x:New_Routing_System</span></a><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">. The link has been added to the landing page. </span></p>', NULL, 1, 335, 1, 530, '2017-08-26 02:09:00', 0, '2017-08-27 02:10:36', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(649, 0, 78, 'Certification Steering Meeting, August 29, 2017', 'certification-steering-meeting-august-29-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-cd8a8ac8-2e12-677d-33f3-55e1dab31b54" dir="ltr">The Joomla! Certification Steering Group meets every Tuesday at 1:00 PM GMT. This meeting was held on August 29, 2017 on Glip.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Team members</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">In attendance</span>: Sam Suresh, Luca Marzo, Andrea Gentil, Chris Keen, Claudia Weber-Lenck, Oscar Ortiz.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Discussion Outline</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Steering Group discussed about the Certification Ambassador idea.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Certification Ambassadors will be enrolled as “contributors” of the Certification Team. A dedicated group will be created in the Joomla! Volunteers Portal.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Group discussed about the involvement of translators, how to qualify, restrictions, requirements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">COT will drop the ticket system on the Certification Website and will create a new public channel on Glip where people can ask information / support about Certification.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Group discussed about the sprint before the Joomla! World Conference: Sam, Luca, Oscar, Andrea, Chris, Richard and Michael will attend the sprint.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Group is working on the goal/agenda document for the JWC Sprint.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Sub-teams reports</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>Certification Operations Team</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">1 JLP pending review. Will be evaluated today.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Oscar evaluated pending JoomlaDays application</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JoomlaDay Texas will host a Certification Exam</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Andrea worked on the newsletters for JLPs (with and without exams)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">COT needs the list of JLPs with and without exams to send out the newsletters (from Platform Team)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">COT would like to ask Steering approval on the Certification Ambassadors Document</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Andrea is working on the new JLP Directory on the Certification website.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">COT proposes to remove the ticket system on the Certification website. Support will be provided through Glip and Email.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>Certification Platform Team</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Working on importing existing questions into QMS by Michael. No progress yet.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Once the questions will be imported, translations could start.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>Certification Marketing Team</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Starting to promote September exams</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Prepared the JLP newsletter</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>Certification Exam Team</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Discussed the QMS progress / status</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">CET wrote guidelines to recruit and onboard new members</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Meeting ends after 55 minutes.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Communication to all Joomla! Learning Partners</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">We are building new Joomla! Learning Partners Directory on certification.joomla.org . Please be patient while we work on it.</p>', NULL, 1, 336, 1, 669, '2017-08-29 12:58:04', 0, '2017-08-29 12:59:17', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(650, 0, 78, 'The Joomla! Certification Ambassadors Initiative', 'the-joomla-certification-ambassadors-initiative', '<h2 id="docs-internal-guid-b335a3a8-2e5d-baaa-9076-ed4712300ff1" dir="ltr">The Context and the Regional Coordinators</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The <strong>Joomla! Certification Program</strong> tried to build a reliable network of partners with Local Communities and Companies in many countries. We created a strong relationship with many Joomla! User Groups, JoomlaDay organizers and with our Joomla! Learning Partners, to spread the Joomla! Certification Program worldwide.</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">In addition to our partners we tried to create a network of “Agents” in different countries, the so called Regional Coordinators, whose aim should be to provide support to the local community of JUGs and JLPs to better deploy and operate the Certification Program in each of the involved countries.</p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Certification Ambassadors</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The “<strong>Regional</strong>” setting sometimes has been intended as a limit for our proud collaborators and contributors, so, today we’re happy to announce the new Joomla! Certification Ambassador role.</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The <strong>Certification Ambassador</strong> is one who want to contribute to the Certification Program spreading the voice and helping people to find useful information about it, providing basic support to the exam session organizers and also supervising exam sessions wherever possible.</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The aim of this initiative is to remove the “regional” limitation and allow our Ambassadors to help the Program wherever they are, for example when they are in events outside their country.</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Obviously, the Certification Ambassador will have a close relationship with the Certification Program Teams to be up to date with all the useful information.</p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Responsibilities</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Being “<em>facilitator</em>” between the JCP Team and the partner network</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Act as Exam Supervisor when needed</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Spread the voice/news about the Joomla! Certification Program</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Report to the JCP Team eventual issues/frictions/concerns given from partners to improve the Program.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Requirements</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Be a Joomla! Exam Certified user</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Willing to contribute at least 5 hours per month for support, survey and others where required</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Who can be Certification Ambassador?</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">We will get in touch with all the first certified people in one Country to invite them become a Certification Ambassador. All the previous involved Regional Coordinators will be approached to “convert” their role in Ambassadors.</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><em><strong>Together we can create a successful Certification Program all over the World.</strong></em></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">If you have any questions, feel free to reach us at <a href="mailto:certification@community.joomla.org">certification@community.joomla.org</a><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p>', NULL, 1, 337, 1, 669, '2017-08-29 14:20:17', 0, '2017-08-29 14:21:50', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(651, 0, 19, 'COT - Meeting Notes - August 31, 2017', 'cot-meeting-notes-august-31-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-b958b78e-384e-da22-7d78-19ea37d65cc9" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The Joomla! Certification Operations Team (COT) meets every Thursday at 1:00 PM GMT. This meeting was held on August 31, 2017, on Glip.</span></p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #434343; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Team members</span></h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #ff9900; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">In attendance</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">: &nbsp;Luca Marzo, Arjen Schrijvers, Oscar Ortiz, Todd Woodward, Pablo Pantoja, Andrea Gentil, </span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #ff9900; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Absent</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">: Chris Keen, Hector Mansilla, Richard van Tilborg. </span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Discussion Outline</span></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Joomla! Learning Partners Directory. Andrea Gentil is working on it. If available, please help her.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Steering Group approved the Certification Ambassadors Initiative. News published at </span><a href="teams/certification-team/reports/650-the-joomla-certification-ambassadors-initiative" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">https://volunteers.joomla.org/teams/certification-team/reports/650-the-joomla-certification-ambassadors-initiative</span></a><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">1 Pending JLP application, on hold due to trademark violations.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Team discussed the new Ambassadors Initiative, how to raise awareness of the program through the first certified people in each country.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Arjen to work on the Ambassadors candidates list.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Andrea will be responsible for the Ambassadors Initiative.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Team discussed the Certification Exam Session that will take place at the Joomla! World Conference in Rome.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Upcoming exam sessions:</span><a href="https://certification.joomla.org/exam/calendar" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #1155cc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">https://certification.joomla.org/exam/calendar</span></a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 2.38452; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">All of these meeting notes are not final and cannot be used as a reference.</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Meeting ends after 35 minutes.</span></p>\r\n<p><br /><br /><br /></p>', NULL, 1, 338, 2, 1459, '2017-08-31 12:40:05', 1459, '2017-08-31 12:43:38', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(652, 0, 10, 'Moving Ahead', 'moving-ahead', '<p style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; color: #000000; font-family: proxima-nova, \'Helvetica Neue\', HelveticaNeue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 15px;">In order to continue the work started some weeks ago about improving the promotion of our properties, Mike joins SM team on Monday 21st August and started helping us with copywriting (high priority for Training – training campaign to be launched on Sept. 1/17)</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Discussion to happen about making the Facebook Group an official channel</li>\r\n<li>More posts and more varied posts are shared. Results are good and stats are increasing - improved interactions and shares.</li>\r\n<li>Team under reorganisation in order to find the best internal process before looking for a new team contributor.</li>\r\n<li>In order to be pro-active, each team lead will be contacted to check their needs and try to improve communication between teams</li>\r\n<li>Decision to come about unmaintained Twitter Accounts: &nbsp;<a href="https://docs.joomla.org/Social_Media_Working_Group#Twitter_Accounts_run_by_other_parts_of_the_Joomla_Project" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #729e52; cursor: pointer;">https://docs.joomla.org/Social_Media_Working_Group#Twitter_Accounts_run_by_other_parts_of_the_Joomla_Project</a></li>\r\n<li>Looking at under performing accounts like Pinterest&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Coordinate with Sander the Joomlers Twitter Account to be used to improve communication about the VP and share all reports, highlight teams, open roles … (waiting for his answer)</li>\r\n<li>3.8 teasing campaign has started</li>\r\n<li>Considering using our Flickr account for JWC and JAB event photos as general repo</li>\r\n<li>Thank you Campaign for partners and sponsors on SM - Lukas will submit to Sandra a specific template for the campaign</li>\r\n<li>Promotion of non-Joomla events where Joomla will be representing such as, CMS Summit, World Hosting Days, Summer Open Source Sprint, PHP LocaWeb</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, 1, 339, 1, 621, '2017-09-01 14:24:45', 0, '2017-09-01 14:39:44', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(653, 58, 0, 'OSM, Inc. - Full Board Meeting - August 31, 2017', 'osm-inc-full-board-meeting-august-31-2017', '<h2 id="docs-internal-guid-cc1617df-4db1-5f84-3718-a200a7044208" dir="ltr" style="text-align: center;">Open Source Matters, Inc.<br />Full Board of Directors and Officers Meeting</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Date</span>: August 31, 2017</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Time</span>: 17:00 UTC</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Total time of meeting</span>: 1 hour 40 minutes</p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr">Attendees:</h4>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert Jacobi (President), Aleksander Kuczek (Vice President), Luca Marzo (Secretary), Mike Demopoulos (Treasurer), Rowan Hoskyns-Abrahall (Director), Michael Babker (Director), Radek Suski (Director), Yves Hoppe (Director), Peter Martin (Director), Søren Beck Jensen (Director), Sandra Thevenet (elected Director).</p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Discussion outline</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sandra Thevenet attended this meeting as newly elected Marketing &amp; Communication Department Coordinator (Director), currently in handover period.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">President</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert shared some progress about sponsorships.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert asked information about possible swag for JoomlaDays.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Treasurer</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Mike fixed the issues with PayPal.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Tax statements have been signed and filed. Waiting for approval.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Mike shared with the Board the “Budget vs Actual” spreadsheet.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Revenue from advertising below projected. &nbsp;Needs to increase or budget refactored to reflect drop.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Capital Team to work on the revenue assessment and improvement.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">An informal working group, directly reporting to the Treasurer will be created. Luca to publish a call for volunteers in the next few days.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Production Department Report</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Google Summer of Code is approaching the end.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Joomla! 3.8 on schedule</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Lots of activity around Joomla! 4.0</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Legal &amp; Finance Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan shared progress about the preparation of WHD. Brochure, Slide Deck, T-Shirt and other materials are being prepared.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Trademark have been issued by the Indonesian Authority.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Trademark Team new members are still in training, they are currently auditing some websites. Team is updating some processes. The current ticket system will be changed to fix some permission issues that affect the tm.joomla.org website.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert asked a detailed report with advertising revenue splitted per *.joomla.org property</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Luca suggested to convert trademark.joomla.org and licensing.joomla.org to redirects to the main tm.joomla.org website instead of being full copies of the main website.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Luca suggested to use functional IDs / Mailbox instead of personal mailbox when it comes to official matters like trademark applications and so on.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">RFP for Google Domains: 1 proposal received. A motion on that will be actioned via email in few days.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Marketing &amp; Communication Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sandra shared the report from Marketing &amp; Communication Department leadership meeting.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Landing page for Joomla 3.8 is ready.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Accessibility Statement is under review and update.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Team is working on a strategic marketing plan.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Community Translation Team is looking for a new Team Leader.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Leadership change in Social Media Team: Alison Meeks is the new Team Leader, Hans Van Der Meer is the new Assistant Team Leader.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Events Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JWC Program complete. Speakers are completing their profile and talk overview.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Facebook Marketing about JWC will start next week.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JUG Team is reviewing the JUG Directory.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan asked the help of Capital Team to reach out some sponsors for JWC.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Operations Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JED received a number of forum posts and tickets about disappearing reviews. This has been caused because JED uses an external review checker which could only check the reviews after they had been published. JED is migrating this external review checker over to their own server to improve the extension review process.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The JED team will hold a face-to-face meeting on Thursday 16 November just before the Joomla World Conference (JWC) in Rome.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The JED team is continuing on the specifications document for JED4 (new future version of the Extensions Directory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Forum Team has contacted its inactive moderators. If they want to continue helping out, they have to respond before 9th September. After that they will be thanked for their past involvement and removed from the moderator team. After 9th September it will be decided if/which some boards need new moderators</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The JTD team welcomed 3 new volunteers to the team. The JTD found a Template Club that is interested in making available their API to their template data which can be used for development of the JTD. The team will organize a Team Sprint probably in October/November.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The JVP team worked with the Volunteer Engagement Team to implement Peakon integration on the Volunteers Portal. A couple of new volunteers applied to help out in the team. The JVP can still use some more volunteers. See: &nbsp;<a href="teams/volunteers-portal-team#roles">https://volunteers.joomla.org/teams/volunteers-portal-team#roles</a> . &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The JVP team asked about a Standard Operating Procedure regarding getting access to Joomla sites and regarding code changes (which should be done via git and not directly in files on the server).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Programs Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Import into Peakon done. Rowan had another appointment with Peakon today, clarifying open questions and getting the database from our tests cleaned. First round will be out tomorrow.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JET recipients announced: <a href="https://community.joomla.org/blogs/community/3146-jet-recipients-for-jwc-2017-announced.html">https://community.joomla.org/blogs/community/3146-jet-recipients-for-jwc-2017-announced.html</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Joomla! Certification Ambassadors Initiative <a href="teams/certification-team/reports/650-the-joomla-certification-ambassadors-initiative">https://volunteers.joomla.org/teams/certification-team/reports/650-the-joomla-certification-ambassadors-initiative</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Vice President</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Aleksander shared progress about the Joomla! Contributor Agreements working group.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Board discussed JCA and other agreements. Aleksander will have a meeting with Production Department and other parts of the Community.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Secretary</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) Working Group is currently recruiting volunteers. Two subject matter experts have been onboarded yesterday. First assessment will be done in few days. The call for volunteers will be kept open.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Motions taken during this meeting</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017/060 - The Secretary proposes to adjourn the meeting<br /></strong>Proposed by Luca Marzo, seconded by Radek Suski.<br /><em>The motion passed with unanimous consent.</em></p>', NULL, 1, 340, 1, 669, '2017-09-04 16:20:05', 0, '2017-09-04 16:21:12', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(654, 0, 13, '5th September 2017 JUG Team Meeting Minutes', '5th-september-2017-jug-team-meeting-minutes', '<p><strong>In attendance:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Djamel Kherbi<br />Jenn Gress<br />Noemi Sanchez del Rio<br />Rowan Hoskyns-Abrahall</p>\r\n<p><strong>Apologies:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Brian Ronnow</p>\r\n<p><strong>No Show:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Eric Lamy</p>\r\n<p>1. Went over pending listings which was fast because there are none.</p>\r\n<p>2. JUG Directory Review: Djamel is kicking butt and the rest of us are not and so need our butts kicked.</p>\r\n<p>3. Rowan resolved two issues we were having with Maqma and FB feeds. Both now resolved. Thank you, Rowan!</p>\r\n<p>4. JWC logistics. We\'re all good.</p>\r\n<p>Next meeting Djamel Leads and we don\'t know who will take minutes yet.</p>', NULL, 1, 341, 2, 535, '2017-09-05 21:11:28', 535, '2017-09-05 21:14:26', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(655, 0, 6, '2017-08 Statistics', '2017-08-statistics', '<div class="well"><dl class="dl-horizontal"><dt>Timeframe</dt><dd>8/2017</dd><dt>New Posts</dt><dd>3549</dd><dt>New Topics</dt><dd>748</dd><dt>New Users</dt><dd>1409</dd></dl></div>\r\n<div class="well"><dl class="dl-horizontal"><dt>Timeframe</dt><dd>8/2016</dd><dt>New Posts</dt><dd>6060</dd><dt>New Topics</dt><dd>1219</dd><dt>New Users</dt><dd>2155</dd></dl></div>', NULL, 1, 342, 1, 503, '2017-09-01 09:48:00', 0, '2017-09-11 09:49:17', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(656, 0, 44, 'JED Team Meeting - August 25, 2017', 'jed-team-meeting-august-25-2017', '<p class="code-line" style="position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;" data-line="3"><img src="https://cdn.joomla.org/images/sharing/joomla-twitter-card.png" alt="JED Team Meeting - June 30, 2017 " style="max-height: 100%;" /></p>\r\n<p data-line="5">Today the Joomla! Extensions Directory (JED) team met at 2 pm GMT via Glip to discuss our progress of current tasks.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-line="7">\r\n<p data-line="7">In attendance: Jaz Parkyn, Anibal Sanchez, Aleksander Kuczek, Hugh Douglas-Smith, Luca Marzo, Mark Lee and Miron Savan.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-line="9">\r\n<p data-line="9">Absent: Daniel Dubois, Darek Śnieg, Dénes Székely, Markus Bopp, Martin Mueller, Paul Franklin and Sotiris Katsaniotis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 id="jed-full-text-search-2017---search-improvements-candidates" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="11">JED 4 - New System Specification</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-line="13">\r\n<p id="vel-team-organization" data-line="56">New JED will start progressing at the beginning of summer. The new JED build process will be formalised first, specifications to be reviewed with the team for comments, additions and amendments, to plan the general development.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-line="13">\r\n<p id="vel-team-organization" data-line="56">The reviews and scoring functionality will remain a closed subject and its code will not present to the JED Devs - only available to JED Team Members.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-line="13">\r\n<p>Jaz has started to plan and define the next version of JED. She\'s been continually working on the specifications doc for the new com_jed, and will soon present it to the team for feedback.&nbsp;Specification doc for JED 4 is nearly done.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>JED Full-Text Search 2017. Search improvements candidates. We are considering Algolia or Elastic Search. No decision yet on the supporting technology.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 id="jed-homepage-2017-updates-jorg-220-and-joomla-372" class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="40">JED Homepage 2017 updates</h2>\r\n<p data-line="46">Following the initial phase, we are working on the&nbsp;second phase:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-line="42">The new design must be applied to other areas of the site. (e.g. the search form located in the inner pages)</li>\r\n<li data-line="43">The new homepage has been successfully implemented. Though, more improvements are required.</li>\r\n<li data-line="49">Recently Added, Top Rated, Most Viewed modules are coming, on incremental small/new changes.</li>\r\n<li data-line="50">New scrolling widgets (similar to Google Play style).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="11">Google Summer of Code 2017: Enhancements to Extension Manager</h2>\r\n<p data-line="33">Anibal has joined the team of mentors. At this time, GSoC EEM is almost over and all the PRs \'ve been submitted to J4 Core. These are the final PRs:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>[4.0] Show changelog - GSoC Expand Extensions Manager</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href="https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17536">https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17536</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>[4.0] Download key manager - GSoC Expand Extensions Manager</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href="https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17575">https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17575</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>[4.0] Fix database for Extensions - GSoC Expand Extensions Manager</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href="https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17537">https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17537</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>[4.0] Edit UpdateSite - GSoC Expand Extensions Manager</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href="https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17553">https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17553</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>[4.0] Checksum extensions - GSoC Expand Extensions Manager</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href="https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17555">https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17555</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>README</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href="https://github.com/joomla-projects/gsoc17_expand_extension_manager/tree/GSoC">https://github.com/joomla-projects/gsoc17_expand_extension_manager/tree/GSoC</a></p>\r\n<p>The Extension Checksum has been backported to Joomla 3.8. Please, help us to test it:</p>\r\n<p><strong>[3.8] - light checksum for </strong>joomlaupdate</p>\r\n<p><a href="https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17632">https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pull/17632</a></p>\r\n<p><span style="color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 22px;">The Review Checking Process</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The efforts to improve the process are ongoing. We expect further additions in the short term. We are already working on an updated review (IP Detective) checker&nbsp; that Hugh is setting up.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 class="code-line" style="font-weight: normal; position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif;" data-line="11">Developer Collaboration Process</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li class="code-line" style="position: relative; color: #1e1e1e; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe WPC\', \'Segoe UI\', HelveticaNeue-Light, Ubuntu, \'Droid Sans\', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;" data-line="29"><em>Migration to Github</em>: Efforts are continuing in this direction.</li>\r\n<li><em>New Wiki</em>: we are documenting the support processes and canned answers in a new Wiki.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, 1, 343, 1, 628, '2017-08-25 17:00:00', 0, '2017-09-11 13:09:46', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(657, 0, 78, 'Certification Steering Meeting - September 12, 2017', 'certification-steering-meeting-september-12-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-b21a4416-7612-b658-ce75-2cd11ef9a61c" dir="ltr">The Joomla! Certification Steering Group meets every Tuesday at 1:00 PM GMT. This meeting was held on September 12, 2017 on Glip.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Team members</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">In attendance</span>: Sam Suresh, Luca Marzo, Andrea Gentil.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Discussion Outline</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Steering Group discussed about the need to build a network of JUGs that provide the Certification across the world.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sam proposed to write a monthly article for JCM including the Certified Users of the month.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Since Certification Team receives a notification every time a new event is approved, CMT will reach out the event organizer to propose a Certification session and, in case of potential issues or difficulties, the team could follow up and eventually send a Supervisor.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Steering Group discussed about the subteam reports and activities.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Sub-teams reports</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>Certification Operations Team</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan Hoskyns-Abrahall has been onboarded</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Andrea and Rowan are working on the JLP Directory</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rowan is trying to replicate the structure they use with the JUG Directory, solving the long-term issue we had between the application workflow and the approved JLP Directory. In this way, the application form could automatically populate the fields required by the listing in the JLP Directory and we can allow them to work on their listing, once approved. (As per the JUG Directory) So &nbsp;we will have finally also a link between the JLP listing page and the exam arranged by such JLP.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The JLP Directory will include also a map showing active JLPs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">This will reduce also the need for the com_workflow to manage the COT Workflow.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">I talked with Rowan (as Events Dept. Director) about the possibility to integrate a badge in the JUG Directory to publicly show the JUGs enabled to provide the Joomla! Certification Exam, this will help to increase the "exposure" of the Certification Program.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">This badge could be provided also to JoomlaDay Organizers when they provide the exam at their events.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">COT received some complaints from RCs / Ambassadors, because of the unclear process to request a session for JUGs. So COT is collecting some inputs and feedbacks to create a better documentation for it and make them happy.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>Certification Platform Team</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sam and Nicky are working on the training material for Supervisor. A draft to be shared next week.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sam is working on the question import in the QMS to start the translation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Link to purchase exam seats for the Joomla! World Conference will be provided during this week.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>Certification Marketing Team</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Andrea is working on the JLPs surveys.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Team is working on the Certification website.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Meeting ends after 30 minutes.</p>', NULL, 1, 344, 1, 669, '2017-09-12 12:30:52', 0, '2017-09-12 12:31:54', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(658, 53, 0, 'Marketing & Communication Department Report from September 2017', 'marketing-communication-department-report-from-sep', '<p dir="ltr">The Marketing Team will try to find all Cloud Services for WebApps like Microsoft Azure, aws, digital ocean, ovh etc. Then find responsible persons, improve description of Joomla! And try to improve ratings. The team is also considering to restart the Distribution Working Group.</p>\r\n<p>The Marketing Onboarding Group is not very active at the moment. The team needs a dedicated mentor who would be capable of doing this job frequently.</p>\r\n<p>The team is preparing for Joomla 3.8 release. Due to unfortunate absence of Sandra, Mike is going to take care about release post. Additionally a blog post about the new router is going to &nbsp;be published.</p>\r\n<p>The Social Media Team continues to work as usual. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Community Translation Team continues to work as usual. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Current progress of its work can be monitored at Crowdin</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr"><a href="https://crowdin.com/project/joomla-3-landing-page/activity_stream">Joomla! 3 Landing page translation</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr"><a href="https://crowdin.com/project/joomla-official-sites/activity_stream">Official Joomla! websites translation</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr"><a href="https://crowdin.com/project/joomla-official-websites-templates/activity_stream">Official Joomla! templates translation</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr"><a href="https://crowdin.com/project/joomla-patchtester/activity_stream">Official Joomla! extensions translation</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr"><a href="https://crowdin.com/project/joomla-marketing-visuals/activity_stream">Joomla! marketing visuals translation</a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><br /><br /></p>', NULL, 1, 345, 1, 449, '2017-09-14 08:03:08', 0, '2017-09-14 08:03:59', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(659, 0, 7, 'Marketing Report - September 2017', 'marketing-report-september-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-68b1e3f8-8557-2f9d-7b25-53e7f5cdb6b2" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="background-color: transparent; color: #000000; font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt;">The Marketing Team is working on different tasks. Because of the vacation time, the last few weeks have been a little quiet. But slowly it\'s back to business.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Volunteers:</span></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Pan to setup a newsletter with Marketing Volunteers and send a regular Newsletter.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">The goal is to engage the volunteers and highlight some github Projects</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Project Management:</span></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Our regular meetings are two times a month.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Tasks &amp; Projects</span></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">The last weeks are mainly for prepare the launch of Joomla 3.8</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">The blogpost for the stable Release ready</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">The Landing Page for Joomla 3.8 is also ready</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">We prepared also two articles for the new Router</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">The initial analysis on the How do you Joomla survey has been started</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Plan for the next sixth months</span></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Concentrate on the Joomla 3.8 and Joomla 4.0 Release</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;">Complete detailed survey analysis and publish results</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, 1, 346, 1, 519, '2017-09-15 11:41:09', 0, '2017-09-15 11:41:21', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(660, 0, 21, 'Trademark Team Report - September 15, 2017', 'trademark-team-report-september-15-2017', '<p><em>This report is to announce the progress of Trademark &amp; Licensing Team, no meeting has been held today.</em></p>\r\n<h3>Progress &amp; Achievements</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A new ticket system has been installed, accessible at <a href="https://tm.joomla.org/contact.html">https://tm.joomla.org/contact.html</a>. Ticket system change was necessary due to several technical issues of the previous one.</li>\r\n<li>The old ticket system will be used as internal reference and archive.</li>\r\n<li>All the tickets in the old system that needs to be addressed, will be moved to the new one.</li>\r\n<li>Tickets will be organized in 3 categories: Trademark Requests, Domain/Website Requests, Audit / Complaints.</li>\r\n<li>The ticket categorization reflects the new structure of the team that will have Trademark Specialists, Domain Specialists, TM Auditors.</li>\r\n<li>Luca, Jenn and Deb will cover Trademark and Domain sections while we onboard other team members.</li>\r\n<li>Claire, Ugur and Subodh are working as Auditor and their training is almost at the end.</li>\r\n<li>TM Auditors and Luca worked on a new version of the audit form used to perform the compliance analysis and verification of websites that use one of the Joomla! Trademarks.</li>\r\n<li>Jenn and Luca worked on a "Trademark Policy for new TLD domains", in order to regulate the registration of domains that includes one of the Joomla trademarks. This document has been submitted to the OSM Board of Directors for evaluation and approval.</li>\r\n<li>The call for volunteers will be open, so new volunteers are welcome to join us in this rebuilding process! </li>\r\n<li>Volunteers can submit their application simply writing an email to <a href="mailto:trademark@opensourcematters.org">trademark@opensourcematters.org</a></li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, 1, 347, 1, 669, '2017-09-15 16:54:01', 0, '2017-09-15 17:10:51', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(661, 58, 0, 'OSM, Inc. - Full Board Meeting - September 14, 2017 ', 'osm-inc-full-board-meeting-september-14-2017', '<h2 id="docs-internal-guid-59a05656-93ff-1a26-8fab-f25f88c7e527" dir="ltr">Open Source Matters, Inc.<br />Full Board of Directors and Officers Meeting</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Date</span>: September 14, 2017</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Time</span>: 17:00 UTC</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Total time of meeting</span>: 1 hour 10 minutes</p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr">Attendees:</h4>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert Jacobi (President), Luca Marzo (Secretary), Mike Demopoulos (Treasurer), Rowan Hoskyns-Abrahall (Director), Radek Suski (Director), Yves Hoppe (Director), Peter Martin (Director), Søren Beck Jensen (Director).</p>\r\n<h4 dir="ltr">Apologies:</h4>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Aleksander Kuczek (Vice President), Michael Babker (Director)</p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Discussion outline</h2>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">President</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">A new sponsorship contract has been signed.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert suggested to have an Account Manager in place to manage sponsor contracts. Søren to lead this initiative.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert shared progress about WHD. Further details at the next Board Meeting.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Production Department Report</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">3.8 remains on schedule</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Accessibility team getting well organized</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Work on 4.0 continues</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Legal &amp; Finance Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">We have a real lawyer (Thomas Grønbek Andersen) who has joined the legal team. He is hoping to recruit a US lawyer to give us more legal oversight in both territories.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Trademark Team has a new ticket system. Rowan installed Maqma for consistency with other joomla.org properties, Luca configured and published it. Only the tickets that need to be processed will be moved to the new system.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">New Trademark Team contributors have been onboarded into the new ticket system. The new model includes 3 main roles: Domain Specialists, Trademark Specialists, Trademark Auditors. Claire is helping writing down a new procedure for violations including notification templates.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">TM Team received an application for joomla.cafe, with lots of connected questions. Jenn Gress handled it, Luca supported. Ticket is still ongoing.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Marketing &amp; Communication Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Radek proposed to support a crowdfunding to support Joomlers affected by the Irma Hurricane.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Noreen is starting her report. &nbsp;She will interview previous marketing leads first and then look to talk to all stakeholders starting from the board and working her way down.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Events Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JUG Team is working properly, no outstanding issues.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Events Team is looking to move events directory from Sobi to DP Calendar in next couple of months. This is so that JUG’s can hook in their Facebook Events, Meetups, Google Calendars and will be more likely to list their meetings if the mechanism to do so is made easier.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Operations Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Joomla forum has contacted inactive moderators, and thanked and removed the ones that did not have time anymore. The team will look for some new moderators for some of the boards.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">JED has relaunched its JED newsletter.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Programs Department</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Yves shared some insights about Peakon results. Further results will be shared after the initial survey round (3 weeks).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Secretary</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Luca shared a document called “Trademark Policy for new Top Level Domains (TLDs)” to regulate the domain name registration that includes one or more Joomla! Trademarks. This document will be reviewed to ensure that all the technical details are covered.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">GDPR Working Group onboarded several people. Yves and Luca worked on a spreadsheet in which there are almost all the applications/services used by the organization with the managed data. A meeting will be held shortly to define next steps and proceed with the assessment.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Treasurer</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Mike is working setting up the Finance Working Group to support his daily job as Treasurer.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Tax filings have been submitted and should be ok.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">The Board is exploring the opportunity to have a line of credit to face operational expenses.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">Motions taken during this meeting</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017/062 - Radek Suski will act as Interim Department Coordinator for Marketing &amp; Communications Department until Sandra Decoux states she is ready to take over the role.<br /></strong>Proposed by Peter Martin, seconded by Søren Beck Jensen<br /><em>The motion passed with unanimous consent.</em></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>#2017-063 - The Secretary proposes to adjourn the meeting<br /></strong>Proposed by Luca Marzo, seconded by Peter Martin.<br /><em>The motion passed with unanimous consent.</em></p>', NULL, 1, 348, 1, 669, '2017-09-18 07:58:16', 0, '2017-09-18 07:59:41', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(662, 0, 25, '2017-09 Joomla! Bug Squad Team Meeting', '2017-09-joomla-bug-squad-team-meeting', '<p dir="ltr">Friday, September 15th, 2017, 18:00 UTC on Glip</p>\r\n<div dir="ltr">\r\n<table><colgroup><col width="244" /><col width="49" /><col width="25" /><col width="235" /><col width="49" /><col width="24" /></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan="6">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Attendees</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan="2">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Niels Braczek (NB)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">X</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td colspan="2">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Demis Palma (DP)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan="6">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Members</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Achal Aggarwal</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jennifer Marriott</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Anja Hage</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Kevin Griffiths</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">256</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Beat</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Leo Lammerink</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">571</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Brian Teeman</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">2390</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Michael Babker (MB)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">1325</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">X</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Chris Davenport</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Nicholas K. Dionysopoulos</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">33</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Constantin Romankiewicz</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Nicola Galgano (NG)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">351</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">X</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">David Steltz</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">35</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Niels van der Veer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">55</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Dimitris Grammatikogiannis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">403</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Peter Martin</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">90</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Duke Speer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rishi Vishwakarma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">George Wilson</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">1098</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Robert Deutz</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">324</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Gunjan Patel</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Roland Dalmulder</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">166</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Harald Leithner</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Ruchika Nagarkar</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Hervé Boinnard</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Shreyas B</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jean-Marie Simonet</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">901</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Tarun Jacob</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jacob Waisner</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Troy Hall (TH)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">72</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jacques Rentzke</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Yaniv Rozenman</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan="6">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Candidates</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Franz Wohlkönig</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">2269</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan="6">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Liaisons</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan="2">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Sandra Thevenet (ST)<br />Documentation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td colspan="2">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Yves Hoppe (YH)<br />Automated Testing</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p dir="ltr">X</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Agenda / Minutes</h2>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">1 Member List</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">The numbers in the table above show the sum of tracker points and number of forum posts within the last three months. Other channels were not evaluated.</p>\r\n<p>The top 5 contributors on the tracker for the last three months were</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Brian Teeman (2334)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Franz Wohlkönig (2268)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Michael Babker (1269)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">George Wilson (1098)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jean-Marie Simonet (848)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Because of the continuous effort Franz is showing, he was invited to become a regular member of the Bug Squad.</p>\r\n<p>Some members did not show activity within the last three months. Due to the rules of this team, they are moved to the honor roll.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Achal Aggarwal</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Anja Hage</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Duke Speer</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Gunjan Patel</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Harald Leithner</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jacob Waisner</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jacques Rentzke</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Jennifer Marriott</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Rishi Vishwakarma</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Ruchika Nagarkar</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Shreyas B</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Tarun Jacob</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">Yaniv Rozenman</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Changes have been made to the members list.</p>\r\n<h3>2 Volunteers Portal</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Members were asked to add their address on the Volunteers Portal. It is a legal requirement for voting members.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">3 PR Priority List</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Nicola proposed to introduce a Top5 list of PRs that are especially important or difficult to test.</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">We want to create (and maintain) a Top10 list, consisting of <a href="https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms/pulls?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Apr+label%3Arelease-blocker">Release blockers</a> and other important PRs. As a starting point, the following list was created:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">17251 Check for ports and make sure we are having local posts (release blocker)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">17952 Regression: Menu forum links conditional (already merged)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr">\r\n<p dir="ltr">17823 Calendar Today: Items wrongly set to pending (look especially for side effects!)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">4 Miscellaneous</h3>\r\n<p>Nothing.</p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr">5 Next Meeting</h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Regular team meeting each month on the 3rd Friday at 18:00 UTC on Glip,</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir="ltr">next time Friday, October, 20th</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, 1, 349, 1, 625, '2017-09-18 13:02:44', 0, '2017-09-18 13:18:06', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(663, 0, 78, 'Certification Steering Team Meeting 19 September 2017', 'certification-steering-team-meeting-19-september-2', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-6e9d4a27-9a2d-e44d-9777-7c6703105961" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The Joomla! Certification Steering Group meets every Tuesday at 1:00 PM GMT. This meeting was held on September 19, 2017 on Glip.</span></p>\r\n<h1 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 20pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Team members</span></h1>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">In attendance: </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Sam Suresh, Luca Marzo, Andrea Gentil. Richard van Tilborg</span></p>\r\n<h1 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 20pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Discussion Outline</span></h1>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">The questions in new QMS imported. However there is an issue with True False questions. Michael to look into it. Sam will initiate re-import after the issues are fixed.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Exam team to decide on timeline for Italian exam the Luca to start the translation.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Marketing team to work on a special page for JWC exam purchase page.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Effective 1 October, all supervisors required to take supervisor course and complete self assessment before able to supervise any exams.</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.999999999999998pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Sub-teams reports</span></h2>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #434343; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Certification Operations Team</span></h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- Follow up with JLPs to get the survey filled out.</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- Andrea is reaching out all the first certified users to promote the Ambassadors Initiative.</span></p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #434343; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Certification Platform Team</span></h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- Questions were imported into QMS</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- To fix issue with TF import</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- working on Supervisor course and assessment</span></p>\r\n<h3 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #434343; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Certification Marketing Team</span></h3>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- working on ideas to reach JDay organizers and JUGs</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- creating a newsletter to reach out all the first certified users to promote the Ambassadors Initiative.</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: \'Open Sans\'; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">- contacted Alison from Social Media Team to have greater exposure</span></p>\r\n<p><br /><br /></p>', NULL, 1, 350, 1, 813, '2017-09-19 12:44:47', 0, '2017-09-19 12:48:13', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(664, 0, 13, '19th September 2017 JUG Team Meeting Minutes', '19th-september-2017-jug-team-meeting-minutes', '<p><strong>In attendance:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Djamel Kherbi<br />Brian Ronnow<br />Jenn Gress<br />Noemi Sanchez del Rio<br />And Rowan via Glip</p>\r\n<p><strong>No Show:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Eric Lamy</p>\r\n<p>1. Discussed directory review. Djamel has completed the review of Africa except a couple. Jenn to do Djamel\'s listing and Noemi taking care of Blida. The rest of the team needs to get on it. Hands were slapped.</p>\r\n<p>2. The only pending listing isn\'t really a pending listing. It\'s approved but we have a JUG that wants to use a TLD. Jenn and Luca are working on a procedure for TLDs at this time.</p>\r\n<p>3. Next meeting is 3 October and Jenn will lead and Brian will take minutes.</p>', NULL, 1, 351, 1, 535, '2017-09-19 21:01:40', 0, '2017-09-19 21:04:54', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(665, 0, 22, 'JWC Meeting Minutes - 19th September 2017', 'jwc-meeting-minutes-19th-september-2017', '<p id="docs-internal-guid-36285c5c-bde3-3cbf-cdf5-0b97178d17c6" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Participants:</span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Ronni K. Gothard Christiansen, MikeDemo, Alison Meeks, Rowan </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Hoskyns-Abrahall, </span>Davide Messia, Roberto Longo</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Apologies: </span><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Hugh Douglas-Smith</span></p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">TEAM ROLES &amp; RECRUITMENT</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Ronni</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c601-36be-1193-9edeeb2ab0c9" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Team requires additional assistance with SoMe, Ronni K. Gothard Christiansen to reach out to volunteers.<br /><br />Further resources to be taken from the Capital Team<br /></span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;"></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">VENUE</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 27pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">Rowan Hoskyns-Abrahall and Davide Messia discussing final details direct with venue.\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">KEY DATES</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Ronni</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c606-313c-f922-532d757692d1" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">07/08/17 - Launched JET<br /></span><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c606-313c-f922-532d757692d1" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">19/08/17 - Announce JET - Visa Applications open at 90 days out -<br />19/08/17 - </span><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c606-313c-f922-532d757692d1" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Call for Speakers Closes</span></p>\r\n<p><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c606-313c-f922-532d757692d1" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">31/08/17 - Full programme Announced - Early Bird Prices Start</span></p>\r\n<p><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c606-313c-f922-532d757692d1" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">30/09/17 - Regular Pricing begins<br /></span></p>\r\n<p><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c606-313c-f922-532d757692d1" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">20/10/17 - Estimated Final Numbers to Venue<br /></span></p>\r\n<p><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c606-313c-f922-532d757692d1" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">03/11/17 - Final Numbers to Venue<br />17/11/17 - JWC Begins</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">TICKETS / PACKAGES</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Rowan</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;"><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c607-1f76-a282-bb3a9b9e4f54" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Ronni to reach out to Joomla.IT<br />The team will continue to meet and liaise with all groups, particularly the Italian groups.<br /></span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 21pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">TRANSLATIONS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Rowan</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c607-dc90-a5e6-4d21fa9db8ce" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Translations of sessions is in progress, negotiations on final model are ongoing.<br /></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">WEBSITE</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Rowan</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">Sponsor profiles and sessions have been added to the site</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">SPONSORS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Ronni</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">Sponsorship signups are continueing with more than 1100 organisations reached out to.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">SPEAKERS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">JENNIFER</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c60d-5db3-2ea0-a2c105ef54c5" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.284; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">All speakers have been contacted, just waiting on a couple of final descriptions.<br /></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">MARKETING</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">HUGH</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c60a-7ed6-6ca5-7f1c949a77ad" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Email templates have been generated to distribute out over next few weeks. Focus to start with speakers list, then advance warning of early bird ticket price deadlines followed by further focus on keynote speakers and content.<br /></span></p>\r\n<p>A range of blogs have been produced and are being published across various media channels</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">SoMe</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">SANDRA</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span id="docs-internal-guid-36285c5c-bdf7-2bfc-6715-86c2a61b560b" style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">SoMe Images for speakers and sponsors: Report from Rowan rec’d and commencing with creation of graphics for all SoMe channel promotions. Pasquale will be assisting with translation so that they are done bilingual.<br /></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Outreach</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">ROBERTO<br /></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span id="docs-internal-guid-e8bd64d5-c60b-8269-71d1-15ab6d659a2b" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;">Email template has been prepared for schools. <br /></span></p>\r\n<p>Davide and Ronni are working on outreach model for communities</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">MISC</span></td>\r\n<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: #efefef; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;"><strong>ALL</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 23pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">Next meeting Tue 26th September</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style="height: 0pt;">\r\n<td colspan="2" style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', NULL, 1, 352, 1, 2257, '2017-09-26 11:10:59', 0, '2017-09-26 11:35:55', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
	(666, 0, 80, 'Media Manager code sprint 20. September 2017', 'media-manager-code-sprint-20-september-2017', '<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Sunday 24th September 2017 on KTC Könistgsein in Frankfurt, Germany</span></p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Goal</span></h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The main goal of the sprint was to stabilize the media manager to be ready for the first Alpha release of Joomla 4. Additionally we added some visual improvements and new features. As the sprint happens on the Joomla day Germany we wanted to get as much direct feedback as much possible from Joomlers on the conference.</span></p>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Day 1</span></h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">We started the day with some organisation stuff. Mainly to define the most important tasks and assign them to people. For that we had set up a simple kanban board which always reflected the progress of the sprint.</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/Eq2wjgotXd-3WrH0FgiOxgrQOC7RQ8TS-O09rXWzZCFDnYRMm9XX2TxAPFAtuxotsYBFPrapaFcjMAiPgUqvmx4ncvNa0ud27bwIjDjn61JEWNnnxuhUHjBYEVFfN5XEh4LF5jpu" alt="20170920_105056.jpg" width="624" height="468" style="border: none; transform: rotate(0.00rad); -webkit-transform: rotate(0.00rad);" /></span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><b id="docs-internal-guid-e45c0595-c363-e336-6c65-a4871157e838" style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.3800000000000001; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The following list shows the merged pull requests from day one:</span></p>\r\n<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.9871999999999999; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><b style="font-weight: normal;">&nbsp;</b></p>\r\n<ul style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">\r\n<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: none; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: